# Line endings are declared here, not left to the consumer's git configuration.
#
# Every text file is LF in the repository and LF in the working tree on every
# platform. The scripts in this tree are COPYed into Linux images and run by bash
# there, and Git for Windows installs with core.autocrlf=true in its SYSTEM
# gitconfig — so without this file a Windows clone checked every script out CRLF
# and a consumer's devcontainer build died at `set: pipefail: invalid option name`.
# Extension-less scripts (Tools/hooks/*) and the .py tools are covered by the
# wildcard; nothing here is enumerated by name so that the next script is covered
# on arrival.
* text=auto eol=lf
